{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from","id":987232,"title":"Can Kindred Sense what clan another is from ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T06:53:58-07:00","id":987232,"title":"Can Kindred Sense what clan another is from ?","content":"Other then the Nosferatu can kindred sense what clan a kindred is from. I wanted to know because I wanted to make a Mehket who's mistaken for a venture but I don't know if that's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:29:37-07:00","id":987248,"title":"","content":"First of all, you can't &quot;sense&quot; the Nosferatu. I'm guessing that you're going with the whole &quot;all Nosferatu feel creepy / ugly&quot; vibe as a dead giveaway. However, other vampires, possibly even ghouls, don't feel creeped out around the Nos by default. Now, that's not saying that really ugly vampires can't be prejudiced against as &quot;Nosferatu,&quot; but that's just a kind of fanatsy racism that's reacting to one's appearance, rather than any reliable way of detecting clan. Nothing stops non-Nosferatu from developing creepy vibes as well.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, detecting clan can be performed via &quot;A Taste of Blood&quot; sidebar of the Kindred Senses section. Bloodhound can pick out details by smelling blood instead of tasting it, and Acute Senses / Distinguished Palate can modify the roll to make it very easy to succeed at. Now, if that means that you have to actively bleed out vitae first, or if you can just sniff another and find out, you'll have to ask your ST, as I'm sure they'll have different ways that they'll have Bloodhound work.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there's the small detail of Blood Sympathy. This is probably your biggest issue, since its fairly easy for Mehket or Ventrue to try and sense a clan tie. If any Ventrue at any time tries to use Sympathy to get a read on your emotions? Its going to be clear to that person you're not a Lord or Lady. It shouldn't be too much of an issue if you're just aiming to be mistaken as a Ven and not actually promoting yourself as one or trying to push any kind of clan bonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:54:20-07:00","id":987253,"title":"","content":"I'd say disguising your blood ties and/or the &quot;flavor&quot; of your Clan in your blood would make a great Devotion, Scale, or Blood Sorcery ritual though.<br /> <br /> Actually that was pretty much what Coil of Blood 4 did in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:22:47-07:00","id":987265,"title":"","content":"The character in question won't be able to conceal their clan from other Mekhet, convince anyone with Auspex 2 or decieve other Ventrue that he is one.<br /> Other kindred can make an accurate guess to someone's clan by observing them but not universally so. It's probable but not likely that anyone other than a Gangrel will turn into a coyote. The guy over in the corner who literally has bar patrons waiting on him hand and foot and are shoving each other out of the way while doing it is most likely Daeva. The one lurking unnoticed in the corner systematically staring at everyone in the room is a Mekhet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-14-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:03:24-07:00","id":987285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987265#post987265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character in question won't be able to conceal their clan from other Mekhet, convince anyone with Auspex 2 or decieve other Ventrue that he is one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I don't see &quot;what Clan is this person?&quot; in the sample questions, which means it's an ST call whether that's a permissible question or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987265#post987265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other kindred can make an accurate guess to someone's clan by observing them but not universally so. It's improbable but not likely that anyone other than a Gangrel will turn into a coyote. The guy over in the corner who literally has bar patrons waiting on him hand and foot and are shoving each other out of the way while doing it is most likely Daeva. The one lurking unnoticed in the corner systematically staring at everyone in the room is a Mekhet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this sort of stereotyping is exactly what makes it possible to pass as a Ventrue, barring supernatural methods of detection, which, granted, vampires are dripping with, but that's why you invent a Devotion or a Scale or a ritual or something to counter them. That's the information arms race vampires are constantly embroiled in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:29:15-07:00","id":987375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987285#post987285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, I don't see &quot;what Clan is this person?&quot; in the sample questions, which means it's an ST call whether that's a permissible question or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the book says the sample list isn't all inclusive, and that the power's description says it's to be used to detect secrets &quot;Is this person deliberately lying about or purposely misrepresenting his clan identity?&quot; and when the answer is affirmative a follow up question along the lines of &quot;Which clan is he impersonating?&quot; certainly falls under the venue of allowable questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987285#post987285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this sort of stereotyping is exactly what makes it possible to pass as a Ventrue, barring supernatural methods of detection, which, granted, vampires are dripping with, but that's why you invent a Devotion or a Scale or a ritual or something to counter them. That's the information arms race vampires are constantly embroiled in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which was why I said general observation of signature behaviors was accurate (because it is) but not infallible (because it's not) before providing examples. That's the point of generalizations and stereotypes because if they were unreliable they wouldn't exist. And when the impersonator's behavior falls outside expected norms or crosses over into the behavior of another clan or they make one (or more than one, in my experience) egregiously stupid remark to raise suspicion and that's when it's game over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-14-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:39:53-07:00","id":987381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987375#post987375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the book says the sample list isn't all inclusive, and that the power's description says it's to be used to detect secrets &amp;quot;Is this person deliberately lying about or purposely misrepresenting his clan identity?&amp;quot; and when the answer is affirmative a follow up question along the lines of &amp;quot;Which clan is he impersonating?&amp;quot; certainly falls under the venue of allowable questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one interpretation, sure, but ultimately what questions beyond the examples will or won't be allowed depends on the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/987232-can-kindred-sense-what-clan-another-is-from?p=987375#post987375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which was why I said general observation of signature behaviors was accurate (because it is) but not infallible (because it's not) before providing examples. That's the point of generalizations and stereotypes because if they were unreliable they wouldn't exist. And when the impersonator's behavior falls outside expected norms or crosses over into the behavior of another clan or they make one (or more than one, in my experience) egregiously stupid remark to raise suspicion and that's when it's game over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess? Seems like stereotypes would work more in the impersonator's favor than against it to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:24:58-07:00","id":987443,"title":"","content":"Auspex 2 seems to sniff out dark secrets and weaknesses to use as leverage or manipulation material. I don't think that this feels like something that Auspex would touch on. Plus, let us be completely honest. I can't see any vampire bothering to waste a question on this kind of thing even if the ST allowed it. Unless there's a super-secret meeting of only family members going on, who's going to want to ask that kind question in the first place? I wouldn't worry about Auspex in the slightest<br /> <br /> But... information arms race? What? Maybe the Ordo versus Lance when it comes to relics and history of the Kindred people, but that's the only kind of information war I'm familar with? Is there some other kind being implied here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:47:18-07:00","id":987450,"title":"","content":"P99, Detecting Sympathy would let you see if another vampire is within your clan. 'She may also spend a point of Willpower to force sympathy and detect a specific relative, assuming they're within the range alloted by their tie.' Four times removed offers no bonus or modifier, but it encompasses all clanmates and Sympathy can affect clanmates in a mile.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly radar but it's close enough, providing they're in your clan.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:22:43-07:00","id":987502,"title":"","content":"","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:43:33-07:00","id":987744,"title":"","content":"First, ask the ST.<br /> <br /> Auspex, from 2 onward, can detect clan or not. That's a ST's call.<br /> <br /> Clan stereotypes are the most probable sources of clan identification on most chronicles, but they're just stereotypes. Even a person who's ugly as hell and gives bad vibes can be just that and be of any, absolutely any clan (Majesty, by the way, is much more to make creepy people into social stars, than to make it with someone who's already good at it), and a Nos can be beautyful, if a little creepy to common mortals. So that's your main asset, you can easily make the Mekhet similar to any other clan.<br /> <br /> Blood Simpathy won't work every time, specially if the character isn't linked by blood to other Mekhet in the city except by clan, nor claims close blood relations with the local Ventrue. In those cases, the only clue is <u>repeated</u> failure on the part of a particularly persistent Ventrue, or <u>eventual</u> success of a Mekhet.<br /> <br /> On the subject of stereotyping not being completely unreliable, some vampires could just naturally appear other clan without even trying it. A domineering person that obsess for control will be taken for a Ventrue for <u>sure!</u> But such person can be that way simple because she is, she was even before the Embrace. And them be embraced by a Mekhet, making the person a Mekhet herself. So... I thought it obvious, just said because some people I know believe that only a member of the clan would behave in a similar fashion.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that this character will probably work pretty well, mainly because I don't see many kindred even caring enough to look further. Maybe even the character herself thinks she's a Ventrue, depending on her story. Depending on the kindred of the city, even if the character tries to live up as a Ventrue it is possible to the others not even caring, or going further to adopt her properly in the clan at a local level, and that's it. She's like a Ventrue, loyal to Ventrue, and no Mekhet sees her as one of them, so what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}